// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CyberneticControls 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2321533940" "Cybernetic controls"
// DetailString :
"P3990672721" "During your battle with the Devouring Earth creatures, you found many pieces of cybernetic equipment implanted in their bodies. You also ran into some Council agents who seemed to be carrying small transmitters."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - 5thControlData 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P332250863" "Council data"
// DetailString :
"P4178390918" "This data details the Council's plan to control the Devouring Earth creatures by using cybernetic implants linked directly into the creatures' primitive nervous systems. There are several notes stating that the Devouring Earth's creatures do not seem to operate entirely according to biological principles. The report proposes that the creatures' resistance might be due to some sort of supernatural bond with the Earth."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1765702980" "You heard that Congressman Bill Marlowe is visiting the city, right? He's meeting with the City Council, trying to start a program to encourage pro-hero initiatives nationwide. Well, I just learned that a swarm of Devouring Earth monsters is after him! One of his staffers called. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>They need someone reliable to protect the congressmen and his aides from the Devouring Earth.</A> I told them there was no one more reliable than {HeroName}!"
// AcceptString :
"P3808258519" "Protect the congressman and his aides from the Devouring Earth"
// SendOffString :
"P1701736857" "Congressman Marlowe is a big supporter of heroes, but it does seem strange that the Devouring Earth would attack him. After all, he has an excellent environmental record. Perhaps there's something we don't know."

